      "boundary": "Constructivism does not mean discovery learning is the only valid form of teaching, nor does it mean that less teacher explanation and more student trial-and-error are automatically better. When a task requires facts, procedures, or safety requirements to be taught first, direct instruction and demonstration are entirely appropriate. The key question is whether teaching connects with learners’ existing understanding and allows evidence to genuinely participate in revising that understanding.",
