    "module": {
      "intro": "The mechanism of formative assessment can be compressed into one chain: gather evidence while there is still time to change, interpret the evidence, and let it change the next action. Feedback without a subsequent action is not enough to complete the formative process.",
      "diagramTitle": "Evidence Changes the Next Step Before the Work Is Fixed",
      "diagramSteps": [
        "Clarify the quality goal",
        "Gather evidence while the work can still be changed",
        "Interpret the gap shown by the evidence",
        "Change the next action in response",
        "Make the final judgment after completion"
      ],
      "diagramStepNotes": [
        "The standards for the rim, wall, handle, and glaze remain stable, so the problem is not an unclear target.",
        "Test clay from the same batch and at a similar firmness is cut open, making the internal gap visible before the real cup is submitted.",
        "Xiaohe compares two test joints and sees that the internal gap changes with the way the contact surface is prepared, rather than merely receiving another “cracked” result.",
        "Before the common submission deadline, the test joint still shows a narrow gap, so she withdraws the cup from that batch, rejoins it, and allows enough drying time again; the evidence directly changes her action.",
        "After the piece later dries fully, is bisque fired, glazed, and glaze fired, it is still judged against the original standards; formative evidence has not replaced summative assessment."
      ],
      "mapping": [
        "The red string tied on after firing → An accurate judgment of the result, but too late to change that cup.",
        "A test joint made from clay from the same batch → Evidence deliberately gathered while the real work can still be adjusted.",
        "The cut-open joint cross-section → A previously invisible gap becomes evidence that can be interpreted.",
        "Withdrawing the cup from the batch and allowing enough drying time again → The evidence changes subsequent action rather than merely adding another comment.",
        "The formal inspection after firing is complete → Formative and summative assessment can occur in sequence while serving different functions."
      ],
      "boundary": "Formative assessment is not synonymous with frequent testing, early grading, or constant teacher prompting. If evidence is unrelated to the goal, arrives too late, cannot be interpreted, or cannot be acted upon by the learner, it is unlikely to have a formative function. Certification, selection, and final reporting still require appropriate summative assessment.",
      "reflection": "Why did Xiaohe withdraw the fifth cup from that batch before the submission deadline? If she had only the red strings from already-fired cups, would she have had an equally clear next action?"
    },
