    "moduleZh": {
      "intro": "教师察觉不是从一个细节直接跳到“学生真正怎么想”的结论。林老师先注意到页边图与答案之间反复出现的不一致，再通过学生现场的点数动作、不同表征和后续任务形成并修正暂时解释。她最后留下的是下一步要观察的问题，而不是一个全知式标签。",
      "diagramTitle": "从课堂线索到可继续检验的专业判断",
      "diagramSteps": [
        "从大量课堂信息中注意到反复或不一致的细节",
        "把该细节与具体任务和学生行动联系起来",
        "形成暂时解释，但保留其他可能性",
        "设计新的互动或情境收集更多证据",
        "据新增证据调整注意方向与教学回应"
      ],
      "diagramStepNotes": [
        "页边小图原本只是众多背景信息之一，重复出现才使它获得进一步观察价值。",
        "关键证据不是教师的直觉，而是瑞安实际怎样点尺子、怎样走粉笔线以及答案如何变化。",
        "同一个错误答案可能由不同原因产生，同一个正确答案也可能掩盖不同思路，因此解释只能暂时成立。",
        "后续任务既可能支持原判断，也可能暴露新的差异；教师不应只寻找证明自己猜测的证据。",
        "察觉最终要影响回应：决定继续问什么、保留什么痕迹、下一次把注意放在哪里。"
      ],
      "mapping": [
        "反复出现的小梯子 → 一个从背景中被选出来继续关注的线索。",
        "正确答案也伴随同样画法 → 使“只要看对错就够了”变得不充分。",
        "让瑞安现场点尺子 → 用学生行动检验页边图是否与其处理任务的方式有关。",
        "不同学生在粉笔线任务中出现不同组合 → 提醒教师不要把一个观察扩展成全班统一诊断。",
        "把数轴和短尺夹在瑞安作业后面，并留下“换一种表示，他还数线吗？” → 把暂时解释转化为下一次可以继续核查的具体观察任务。"
      ],
      "boundary": "教师察觉受教师知识、经验和注意选择影响，不是对学生思维的直接读取。同一行为可能来自语言、任务理解、表征习惯或其他因素。高质量察觉需要把判断建立在可观察证据上，并允许后续证据推翻或修正先前解释。",
      "reflection": "如果林老师已经把“数线”当成最终结论，而不是准备换一种表示继续核查，她最可能错过什么？"
    },
    "module": {
      "intro": "Teacher noticing does not mean moving directly from one detail to a claim about what a student “really thinks.” Lin first notices a recurring inconsistency between the margin drawing and Rui’an’s answers, then uses his counting actions, different representations, and follow-up tasks to form and revise a tentative interpretation. She ends with a concrete next check rather than an all-knowing label.",
      "diagramTitle": "From a classroom clue to a professional judgment that can still be tested",
      "diagramSteps": [
        "Notice a recurring or inconsistent detail among many classroom events",
        "Connect the detail to a specific task and the learner’s observable actions",
        "Form a tentative interpretation while keeping other possibilities open",
        "Use a new interaction or representation to gather more evidence",
        "Adjust attention and teaching response in light of the new evidence"
      ],
      "diagramStepNotes": [
        "The margin drawing begins as one small piece of background information. Its repetition is what makes it worth following.",
        "The critical evidence is not the teacher’s intuition, but what Rui’an actually does with the ruler, the chalk lines, and his answers.",
        "The same wrong answer can arise from different causes, and the same correct answer can hide different reasoning, so any interpretation must remain provisional.",
        "Follow-up tasks can support an initial interpretation or reveal important differences. The teacher should not design them only to confirm a first guess.",
        "Noticing matters because it changes what the teacher does next: what to ask, what traces to preserve, and what to look for in the next task."
      ],
      "mapping": [
        "The repeated little ladder in the margin → a detail selected from the background for further attention.",
        "The same drawing beside both correct and incorrect answers → evidence that simple right/wrong marking is not enough.",
        "Asking Rui’an to show how he counts on the ruler → using observable action to test whether the drawing is related to how he handles the task.",
        "Different answer patterns in the chalk-line activity → a reminder not to turn one observation into a single diagnosis for the whole class.",
        "Tucking a number line and ruler behind Rui’an’s work and writing “If the representation changes, does he still count the lines?” → turning a tentative interpretation into a concrete next observation."
      ],
      "boundary": "Teacher noticing is shaped by teachers’ knowledge, experience, and attention; it is not direct access to a student’s mind. The same behavior can reflect language, task interpretation, representational habits, or other factors. High-quality noticing therefore rests on observable evidence and remains open to revision when later evidence points elsewhere.",
      "reflection": "If Lin had already treated “counting the lines” as the final diagnosis, what might she miss by not testing the same idea with a different representation?"
    },
