      "diagramStepNotes": [
        "The fourteen pages, twenty-four seconds, and automatic loop remain constant throughout, with the sequence clearly running from the Thursday studio version to the first Thursday-evening station test, the second Friday-morning test, and delivery before three on Friday afternoon.",
        "The first passenger enters midway on a rooftop page with no text and still encounters the broken blue line, so the central conflict is not merely text simplification or generic advertising reduction.",
        "The continuous blue line is simply how this particular project uses this screen’s loop and horizontal length; it does not imply that all digital screen works should loop.",
        "The second test does not merely confirm that looping works. It reveals that dense texture and text timing are still mismatched with platform viewing, directly shaping the final revision.",
        "Watercolor, pencil, and paper grain remain in the screen version, while the paper book stays intact, so the story treats neither medium as more advanced, purer, or superior."
      ],
