      "boundary": "Material affordance does not mean that a material has intentions, or that one property automatically dictates one correct form. Action possibilities always depend on purpose, tools, skill, scale, loading, environment, and user. The same polypropylene could behave differently at another thickness, temperature, connection method, or task. This story only shows how one specified sheet behaves differently in sharp-folding and curved tab-and-slot relationships within this lampshade project; it does not provide a universal function list for the material.",
