      "boundary": "Iterative craftsmanship is not blind trial and error, mechanical repetition, or the claim that “persistence guarantees success.” Effective iteration requires information from real use to change the next making decision in a specific way. The story also does not turn “change one variable at a time” into a universal law: joints, adhesive width, sewing position, guards, and materials can interact in bookbinding. The slightly loose sewing seen in one weekend-used book is only one piece of follow-up evidence and does not justify claiming that the whole batch has a general structural problem.",
