    "conceptName": "Tension and resolution",
    "conceptNameZh": "张力与解决",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "Tension in music and performance often arises when an established pattern, tendency, or expectation is delayed, redirected, interrupted, or reinterpreted; resolution occurs when that expectation is completed, redirected, or given a new point of reference. Meyer and Huron both emphasize that expectation depends on learned patterns and context rather than emerging automatically from simply becoming louder, faster, or denser.",
      "Resolution also does not have to mean a traditional Western tonic chord, nor does it have to mean complete calm. A rhythmic arrival, completion of a movement, return of a timbre, or structural closure can all serve a resolving function within a particular style and context. Lerdahl and Jackendoff’s analysis of tonal musical structure has been historically influential, but their model is primarily based on Western tonal music and should not be treated as a universal rule for all musical cultures."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "音乐与表演中的张力常来自已经建立的模式、倾向或期待被延迟、偏转、阻断或重新解释；解决则是这些期待得到完成、转向或形成新的参照。Meyer 与 Huron 都强调，期待需要来自学习到的模式与上下文，而不是单靠“更响、更快、更密”自动产生。",
      "解决也不必等于传统西方调性里的主和弦，更不必意味着彻底平静。节奏落点、动作完成、音色回归、结构闭合等都可能在具体风格和场景中承担解决作用。Lerdahl 与 Jackendoff 对调性音乐结构的分析具有重要历史影响，但其模型主要以西方调性音乐为对象，不应被当作所有音乐文化的普遍规则。"
    ],
