      "boundary": "Reflective equilibrium is not simply any act of reflection, nor is it an averaging of several intuitions. Case judgments, general principles, and background beliefs must all be open to revision in light of one another and relevant evidence; wider forms also compare alternative principles and background theories. Even if a set of beliefs becomes more coherent, they may still be jointly wrong. Coherence itself does not guarantee truth, and new evidence or objections can reopen the process. The characters, 1998 installation, and archives are fictional. This everyday analogy for ethical judgment does not establish general museum conservation standards.",
      "reflection": "Why, after changing her judgment that the blue card should be removed, does Mei Lin also have to give up the idea of permanently preserving it as “the first participation card”?"
