      "boundary": "The arbitrariness of the sign does not mean that all names are equally good or that individuals can assign meanings however they like. Sound symbolism, iconicity, word formation, historical convention, and internal system relations can all constrain forms; organizational training and labeling also affect how quickly a convention becomes shared. This fictional workshop is only a concrete model and does not empirically establish that all linguistic signs are arbitrary to the same degree.",
