      "boundary": "Archival silence does not have to come from malicious deletion. It may arise from form design, financial purpose, privacy, self-protection, resource limits, damage, accession choices, or later cataloguing. Finding side evidence, more elderly witnesses, or an old list does not automatically restore a complete truth; such materials can only expand, narrow, or redefine what the surviving evidence supports. The evening school, people, and archive in this story are fictional.",
