    "fieldTitleZh": "会计与税务",
    "title": "The €6,000 on June’s Books",
    "titleZh": "六月账上的六千欧元",
    "summary": "On the last day of June, €6,000 has just arrived, but Lin Cheng is still waiting for Shen Yan’s answer: how many workdays can the studio hold for her next month?",
    "summaryZh": "六月最后一天，6,000欧元刚刚到账，林澄却还在等沈妍答复：下个月能给她留多少工作日？",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "On the afternoon of June 30, Shen Yan had to give freelance assistant Lin Cheng a clear answer before evening: could the studio guarantee her three days of work per week in July? Another client was also waiting for Lin Cheng, so she could not keep the time open indefinitely. The studio had just received €6,000, prepaid by a client for a three-month content package covering June through August, and Shen Yan had originally planned to use that cash receipt as the basis for sending “three days a week.”",
      "Shen Yan spread the package contract and the June delivery records beside the schedule. The contract listed €2,000 for each of the three months; the agreed June work had been completed, and the client confirmation email was there. She changed the €6,000 in the monthly report to €2,000 of June revenue, recorded the other €4,000 under advance service payments, and attached the still-unfinished July and August arrangements. The scheduling message she had been about to send remained open, and she moved the cursor back to before the words “three days a week.”",
      "Lin Cheng sent over the folder for the June 28 product shoot and asked which day in the first week of July she should come in to archive the files. Shen Yan opened the client-signed delivery confirmation: the final images had been fully delivered and accepted, while the €1,200 invoice was not due to be issued until July 3 under the contract. She added another €1,200 to June revenue and recorded a receivable. Lin Cheng would still come in that day for file archiving and feedback organization, but the contractual photography delivery had already been completed. Shen Yan left one day on the schedule without moving that revenue into July.",
      "The outsourced retouching completed on June 29 had also been finished and accepted by the studio, while the €700 bill would arrive in July. Because the service had already been consumed in June, €700 was recorded as a June expense and as a payable. Looking only at the three listed items, June revenue was €2,000 + €1,200 = €3,200, and after subtracting the €700 expense the result was €2,500. At the same time, the June net cash inflow from those three items remained €6,000. Neither figure was the company’s total bank balance or full net profit.",
      "Shen Yan deleted the message she had prepared saying “fixed three days a week from July.” Looking at the July projects that were already confirmed, she changed it to a guarantee of eight workdays. On the phone, she read Lin Cheng the dates one by one and agreed to revisit any fixed arrangement for September onward at the end of August. Lin Cheng accepted the eight days and gave two other August dates to another client. Shen Yan sent out the July schedule and added a note to the partners’ brief: the June result from the three items was €2,500 and the net cash inflow was €6,000; other costs and future projects still had to be considered separately.",
      "At the end of the day, Shen Yan received the schedule back from Lin Cheng. Eight July dates were confirmed, and two August dates were marked “other client.” She clipped the schedule behind three supporting documents: the €6,000 package contract, the June 28 acceptance for the €1,200 delivery, and the June 29 completion record for the €700 outsourced work. The message that had said “three days a week” was never sent."
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "六月三十日下午，沈妍要在傍晚前给自由助理林澄一个明确答复：七月是否能保证每周三天的排班。林澄手里还有另一家客户在等，不能一直留着时间。工作室刚收到6,000欧元，是客户预付的六月到八月三个月内容套餐；沈妍原本想凭这笔到账直接把“每周三天”发出去。",
      "沈妍把套餐合同和六月交付记录摊到排班表旁。合同把三个月服务各列为2,000欧元，六月的约定内容已完成，客户确认邮件也在。她把月报里那笔6,000改为六月收入2,000，将另外4,000记到预收服务款下面，附上七月、八月尚未完成的安排。原本准备发出的排班消息还开着，她先把光标退回了“每周三天”之前。",
      "林澄发来六月二十八日的产品拍摄文件夹，问七月第一周哪天来归档。沈妍打开客户签过的交片确认：最终成片已经全部交付验收，1,200欧元按合同到七月三日才开票。她给六月收入再加1,200，同时列出应收。林澄那天仍要来做文件归档和反馈整理，合同要求的拍摄交付却已完成。沈妍在排班表上留下一天，没有把这项收入搬到七月。",
      "六月二十九日的修图外包也已经完成并被工作室接收，700欧元账单会在七月寄来。服务已在六月耗用，所以700计入六月费用，同时形成应付。只看列出的三项业务，六月收入是2,000＋1,200＝3,200，减去700后为2,500；同时，这三项的六月现金净流入仍是6,000。两个数字都不是全公司的银行余额或完整净利润。",
      "沈妍删掉准备发给林澄的“七月起固定每周三天”，对照已确定的七月项目，改成保证八个工作日。她在电话里把能保证的日期逐一念给林澄，并约好八月底再谈九月以后的固定安排。林澄接受八天，把另外两个八月日期给了另一家客户。沈妍将七月排班表发出去，又在合伙人简报中注明：三项业务的六月结果为2,500，现金净流入为6,000；其他成本与未来项目还须另算。",
      "下班时，沈妍收到林澄回传的排班表，七月八个日期已经确认，八月另有两个日期标着“其他客户”。她把这张表夹在三份凭据之后：6,000欧元套餐合同、六月二十八日1,200欧元交片验收、六月二十九日700欧元外包完成单。原来写着“每周三天”的消息没有发出。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Accrual accounting",
    "conceptNameZh": "权责发生制",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "Accrual accounting assigns revenue that has been earned and meets the recognition conditions, and expenses already consumed, to the period in which they occur rather than mechanically following cash dates. Advance receipts for unperformed work create liabilities, earned but uncollected amounts create receivables, and consumed but unpaid costs create payables.",
      "For the three listed items, June revenue is €2,000 + €1,200 = €3,200; after the €700 expense, the result is €2,500. The June net cash inflow from those three items remains €6,000. Neither figure is the company’s total net profit or bank balance."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "权责发生制把已履行且满足确认条件的收入、已耗用的费用归入实际发生期间，不机械跟随收付款日。预收未履约部分形成负债，已赚未收形成应收，已耗用未付形成应付。",
      "本例列出的三项六月收入为2,000＋1,200＝3,200，减700费用为2,500；三项六月现金净流入仍为6,000。两者都不是全公司净利润或银行余额。"
    ],
    "overall": "The same money can arrive before a service is performed or be collected only after delivery. Accrual accounting assigns completed services and consumed costs to the relevant period, so operating performance and cash receipts or payments each answer a distinct question.",
    "overallZh": "同一笔钱可能先于服务到达，也可能在交付后才收到。权责发生制把已完成的服务和已耗用的成本归入相应期间，让经营表现与现金收付各自回答一个清楚的问题。",
