      "boundary": "The two scenarios are limited stress checks, not a probability model, variance estimate, forecast, or specific investment recommendation. Real portfolio risk also depends on weights, volatility, correlation, changing holdings, and other common shocks. These tables cannot prove that one portfolio is definitively better, nor can diversification guarantee returns or prevent losses.",
      "reflection": "When two products from different fund companies hold many of the same assets, how would you distinguish “more fund names” from “more genuinely distinct sources of risk,” and how would you avoid treating two hypothetical scenarios as forecasts?"
