      "boundary": "Record version control is not accomplished simply by renaming files, sorting by time, or using a shared drive, nor does every office need to copy engineering configuration-management systems. The NASA source is an engineering configuration-management reference; the TNA 2007 document is historical conceptual material and is no longer current, so it is not treated as present-day regulation or certification guidance.",
      "reflection": "If a draft inherits the next version’s appearance and QR field and also appears first in search results, which approval, effective, distribution, and on-site-use states would you rely on to determine what can actually be executed today?"
