      "She crosses out “oxygen in excess” and writes beside it, “convert to mol first, then compare n/stoichiometric number for each reactant and take the smaller value.” The page keeps two final boxes: theoretical water, 36.0 g; remaining H2, 4.0 g. The field for actual amount collected remains blank."
