    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Lin Xi, a student in an introductory Earth-science course, is preparing to submit a rock-transformation pathway exercise. The first pathway already gives “weathering and erosion → transport → deposition,” and the current box is explicitly a deposited layer of loose sand. Yet she connects the next arrow directly to sandstone. A second pathway starts from limestone, labels the process “heating,” and places magma in the very next box. She thinks that naming the rock type in the next box is enough to explain the pathway.\n\nShe fixes the sand pathway first. Because the problem has already moved and deposited the sediment into a layer, this specified downstream lithification path does not repeat those upstream steps. What is missing is later burial, followed by compaction and cementation. Lin Xi replaces the short arrow with “burial → compaction/cementation → consolidated clastic sedimentary rock” and labels the two boxes “loose” and “consolidated.”\n\nShe rereads the conditions for the second pathway: under suitable heat, pressure, and related conditions, the limestone undergoes mineral and structural reorganization, but the problem specifies that it does not melt. Lin Xi deletes “heating → magma,” writes “solid-state reorganization” beside the arrow, and changes the next box to marble. The change is in the organization of solid rock rather than a prior transition into melt.\n\nTo check the melt pathway, she separately takes the branch labeled “a rock reaches melting conditions.” Only at that point does the material become magma. Beside the next arrow she writes “cooling and solidification, forming igneous rock.” This usually involves crystallization, but rapidly cooled lava can also form volcanic glass. She does not assign one universal melting temperature because the actual conditions depend on composition, pressure, and other geologic factors.\n\nThe problem finally adds another condition: “this marble is later uplifted and exposed at the surface.” Lin Xi connects that to a branch labeled “can begin to undergo weathering and erosion,” instead of treating uplift itself as a change of rock type. She leaves a separate dashed branch showing that only if melting conditions are later met at depth could the material enter a magma pathway.\n\nBefore submitting, Lin Xi covers the rock-type names and reads only the processes along the arrows. The loose-sand box needs burial, compaction, and cementation; the word “sandstone” cannot supply those missing steps. The limestone label still says “unmelted,” so magma cannot occupy the next box. She checks the branches after marble: uplift and exposure allow weathering, while entering magma still requires the melting conditions written beside the other arrow. Both short arrows are now repaired, and the branches remain separate rather than being joined into one compulsory circle.",
    "storyBodyZh": "地学入门课的学生林汐正准备提交一张岩石转化路线题。第一条路线已经给定“风化侵蚀→搬运→沉积”，当前格明确是一层已沉积的松散砂。她却把下一支箭头直接连到砂岩；第二条路线则从石灰岩写“受热”，下一格就画成岩浆。她以为下一格的岩类名称齐全，路线就已经交代完了。\n\n她先处理松砂。既然题目已经把碎屑搬运并沉积成层，这一支指定的后续成岩路线就不再重复上游步骤；真正缺的是后续埋藏，以及压实和胶结。林汐把短箭头拆成“埋藏→压实/胶结→固结的碎屑沉积岩”，并在两格旁分别写上“松散”和“固结”。\n\n她再读第二条路线的条件：石灰岩在适当热、压力等作用下发生矿物和结构重组，但题目注明没有熔融。林汐把“受热→岩浆”删掉，在箭头旁标“固态重组”，下一格改成大理岩。这里改变的是固态岩石内部组织，不是先变成熔体。\n\n为了确认熔体路线，她另取题目中的“某岩石达到熔融条件”分支。只有这时材料才进入岩浆状态；她在下一支箭头旁写“冷却固化，形成火成岩”，通常会伴随结晶，快速冷却的熔岩也可能形成火山玻璃。她没有给统一熔融温度，因为实际条件取决于岩石组成、压力和其他地质因素。\n\n题目最后另给一个条件：“这块大理岩后来被抬升并暴露在地表。”林汐据此把它接到“可开始经历风化和侵蚀”的分支，而不是把抬升本身写成岩类变化。旁边另留一条虚线：若以后在更深部满足熔融条件，才可能转入岩浆路径。\n\n提交前，林汐先遮住图上的岩类名称，只沿箭头读过程。松砂那一格必须接上埋藏、压实和胶结，不能靠“砂岩”两字补足；石灰岩旁仍写着“未熔融”，下一格便不能放岩浆。她再看大理岩后的分叉：抬升暴露允许它经历风化，要转入岩浆，却还得满足另一支箭头注明的熔融条件。两支短箭头都已改好，图上的分叉没有被重新接成一个必经圆圈。",
    "explanation": "The loose sand in this exercise has already been transported and deposited, so the specified lithification route next adds burial, compaction, and cementation. Loose sand in nature can still be eroded and transported again.\n\nUnder unmelted conditions, limestone can reorganize in the solid state to become marble. Uplift and exposure change environmental conditions rather than instantly changing rock type, and melting requires separate conditions.",
    "explanationZh": "本题中的松砂已经完成搬运和沉积，因此这条指定成岩路线后续补埋藏、压实和胶结；自然界中的松砂仍可能再次被侵蚀搬运。\n\n石灰岩在未熔融条件下可固态重组为大理岩；抬升暴露只改变环境条件，不会立即改变岩类，熔融也需另外满足条件。"
