      "boundary": "The model uses the same time interval and joule units throughout, and the full system is explicitly isolated from external heat, work, radiation, and matter exchange. Chemical energy and other internal-energy accounts must not overlap. Heat Q and work W are transfers across boundaries, not forms stored in an object. A real unclosed energy account must not have its residual forced into the label “heat,” and energy conservation does not guarantee high efficiency or prevent useful energy from decreasing.",
      "reflection": "Why can you infer that total stored energy in the battery subsystem falls by 12 J only after the model explicitly states that the battery’s other internal energy is unchanged?"
