    "overall": "Invariance methods begin by fixing the state space and all legal operations, then proving that a quantity or relation is preserved at every step. The initial state plus stepwise preservation extends to every finite legal sequence. A target with a different invariant value can be ruled out; a target with the same value is merely not excluded by that condition.",
    "conceptName": "Invariance",
