    "overall": "Hierarchical information organization is illustrated here through a fictional design workflow: parent-child directories and component-by-component paths provide location context, allowing identically named files to be distinguished accurately across branches. Paths change when items are manually moved or renamed, so they represent location rather than permanent identity; cross-project references, permissions, and retention rules require other mechanisms.",
