    "overall": "Residence time is illustrated here through a fictional once-through tracer experiment: V/Q provides a nominal space time and, under conditions such as steady flow, an appropriate effective volume, and suitable system boundaries, can serve as an average timescale, while actual fluid exit times form a distribution. An inert-tracer outlet response can describe that distribution, but a binned weighted mean is only an approximation.",
