    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "Young Dr. An needed one successful project before the hospital's winter review. A celebrated controlled trial seemed to provide it: an unnamed treatment had reduced an important future complication on average among eligible participants. She read the abstract between appointments, circled the relative reduction, and enrolled the next suitable-looking patient, roof worker Old Qi. The consent discussion covered the printed points, but she never asked what his working day required. Old Qi accepted because the rainy season was coming and he wanted to remain strong enough to climb thirty ladders a day.\n\nDuring the first week, Old Qi felt a treatment burden that had been listed deep in the paper but not emphasized in Dr. An's explanation. On flat ground it was manageable. Halfway up a ladder, with tiles balanced on one shoulder, it became frightening. He climbed down, drank water, and returned to work because missing a shift meant losing his place on the crew. At review he said only that he was 'fine.' Dr. An recorded adherence and saw the project moving toward its target.\n\nThe next episode came near the roof ridge. Old Qi dropped a tile that shattered beside an apprentice. Nobody was injured, but the foreman removed him from height work without pay. Old Qi brought the broken corner to the clinic and asked why a treatment meant to protect his future had made today's work harder. Dr. An pointed first to the trial average. The tile dust on her desk made that answer sound smaller than it had in the journal.\n\nShe reread the full study. She marked participant selection, comparator, absolute as well as relative effects, uncertainty, adverse outcomes, follow-up, and the conditions under which treatment had been delivered. The research was not false; it answered a narrower question. It contained no row for repeated ladder climbing, no measure of a lost day's wages, and little guidance on whether its average trade-off fit Old Qi's work and priorities. Her pharmacist and senior colleague also saw implementation risks that an abstract could not carry.\n\nAt a new meeting, Dr. An explained what the evidence supported, what remained uncertain, and which clinically reasonable options were available after individualized reassessment. Old Qi described the outcomes he feared and the income his family could survive without. His preference could not turn an ineffective option into an effective one, but it changed which acceptable trade-off mattered. Together with the responsible team, he chose a revised plan and a safer return-to-work arrangement.\n\nDr. An withdrew Old Qi from the hospital's headline project and reported why the original implementation had failed. Her promotion score fell below the line. Old Qi lost three weeks of height-work wages while the plan was reviewed and his function reassessed; the apprentice took his place on the best-paying roof. The better decision did not refund the cost of the first one.\n\nMonths later Old Qi was back on selected roofs under an agreed arrangement, with benefits and burdens still monitored rather than declared settled. Dr. An kept the trial table above her desk. Beneath its printed rows she drew one empty row in red pencil and placed the broken tile corner on it. The row had room for a ladder, a wage packet, and the next patient the paper had never been designed to contain.",
    "storyBodyZh": "年轻的安医生需要在医院冬季考核前做成一个项目。一项著名对照试验像是送来了答案：某项治疗在符合条件的受试者中，平均降低了一个重要的未来并发症。她在两次门诊之间读完摘要，圈住相对降幅，便为看起来合适的下一位患者屋顶匠老齐制定方案。说明谈到了印刷出来的要点，却没人问他的工作每天要爬三十次梯子。雨季将到，老齐想保住体力和工位，很快答应。\n\n第一周，老齐出现论文深处列过、却未被安医生重点说明的治疗负担。站在平地时还能承受，肩扛瓦片爬到梯子中段时却令人发慌。他退下来，喝了水，又继续上工，因为少一个班就可能失去施工队位置。复诊时，他只说“还好”。安医生记录依从情况，以为项目正朝指标推进。\n\n第二次发生在屋脊附近。老齐失手掉下一片瓦，碎片落在学徒脚边，幸好无人受伤，工头却立刻取消他的高处工作，也不发那部分工钱。老齐把一角碎瓦带进诊室，问一项保护未来的治疗为何先毁掉今天的工作。安医生第一反应仍是指向试验平均值。瓦灰落在桌面上，期刊里很大的答案忽然变小了。\n\n她终于读过摘要后面的全部内容，标出受试者选择、对照、绝对与相对效果、不确定性、不良结局、随访和治疗实施条件。研究没有错，它回答的问题更窄。表格没有“每天反复爬梯”这一行，也没有测量一天工钱的损失，更不能直接判断平均取舍是否适合老齐的工作与优先目标。药师和资深同事还看见了一些摘要装不下的实施风险。\n\n重新会谈时，安医生说明证据支持什么、哪些仍不确定，以及个体复评后有哪些临床上合理的选项。老齐说出最害怕的结果，也算清家里能承受多少收入损失。偏好不能把无效措施变有效，却会改变合理选项中哪种取舍最重要。在负责团队参与下，他选择修订后的方案与更安全的返工安排。\n\n安医生把老齐撤出医院宣传项目，如实报告原实施为何失败，她的晋升分数跌出线外。方案复核与功能评估期间，老齐失去三周高处工钱，学徒接走了报酬最高的屋顶。较好的第二次决定，没有退还第一次决定已经花掉的钱。\n\n几个月后，老齐按商定安排回到部分屋顶，收益与负担仍被继续观察，没有人宣布问题永久结束。安医生把试验表留在桌前，在印好的行列下用红铅笔画了一条空行，又把那角碎瓦放上去。空行足够容下一架梯子、一只工资袋，以及下一位从未为那篇论文量身制作的患者。",
