    "explanation": "Continuity of care means that care remains coherent across time, people, settings, and transitions. It includes informational continuity (relevant knowledge follows the patient), relational continuity (a trusted clinical relationship when feasible), and management continuity (plans and responsibilities remain coordinated as needs change). Useful practices include medication reconciliation, clear handovers, shared records, named ownership of pending results, and closed-loop follow-up. Continuity does not require the same professional forever, nor does sending information prove it was received or acted on. It must be adapted to resources, urgency, patient goals, and local systems.",
    "explanationZh": "照护连续性指照护跨越时间、人员、场所和转衔后仍保持连贯，包括信息连续、关系连续与管理连续。常见支点有用药核对、清楚交班、共享记录、为待出结果指定负责人以及闭环随访。它不要求永远由同一人照护，也不能把“资料已发送”当成“已经接收并行动”。具体安排需结合资源、紧急程度、患者目标和当地系统。"
