    "explanation": "Graded exposure is a collaborative, progressive approach used after appropriate assessment to help a person re-engage with feared and avoided situations, sensations, or activities. Repeated, planned experience can test and update threat predictions and restore function. A hierarchy is individualized and flexible; pace, repetition, context, goals, and safety behaviors are reviewed rather than increased mechanically. Exposure is not coercion, flooding, reassurance alone, or removal of precautions against genuine danger, and anxiety need not disappear for learning to occur. Suitability and safety require professional judgment; this fictional sequence is not a self-treatment protocol.",
    "explanationZh": "分级暴露是在适当评估后，以合作、渐进方式帮助个体重新接触所恐惧和回避的情境、感觉或活动。计划性重复经验可检验并更新威胁预测、恢复功能。层级应个体化且可调整，速度、重复、情境、目标与安全行为都需复核。它不是强迫、猛然淹没、只靠安慰或撤掉真实危险的防护；焦虑也不必完全消失才会发生学习。是否适用与安全应由专业判断。"
