    "explanation": "A hierarchy of evidence gives different starting weight to evidence according to the specific question and a design's ability to limit bias and support causal or other inference, rather than applying one rigid universal ranking. Final certainty also depends on conduct, consistency, precision, directness, publication bias, and the whole body. Benefit, rare harm, diagnosis, prognosis, experience, and implementation may require different designs.",
