    "explanation": "The service recovery paradox is a conditional finding: after a limited failure, prompt recovery perceived as fair in outcome, process, and interpersonal treatment can sometimes produce satisfaction or loyalty above an ordinary error-free experience. It is neither reliable nor universal, especially for severe, repeated, or core-service failures. Organizations should prioritize prevention and use recovery for restoration and learning, never intentional failure.",
