    "explanation": "A constraints-led approach manipulates interacting individual, task, and environmental constraints so learners use information, explore, and self-organize functional movement solutions in representative settings. It links perception and action and develops adaptability. It does not mean an absent coach or rejection of technical teaching; safety, representativeness, feedback, inclusion, necessary guidance, and transfer still require professional design.",
